From: Beize <noreply@beize>
Subject: [PATCH] homework: require plaintext recovery keys only for LUKS and fscrypt

Changing the password of a home with a recovery key failed unless the
recovery key was supplied as well ("Missing plaintext recovery key for
defined recovery key"), for every storage type. The plaintext is needed
to propagate secrets into LUKS key slots and fscrypt policies; for
directory, subvolume and cifs homes nothing is propagated, and the
recovery key hashes are kept in the record unchanged.

Authentication is unaffected: home_load_embedded_identity() still
requires the supplied secret to unlock the existing record (the current
password or a recovery key).

Fixes: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/25876

--- a/src/home/homework.c
+++ b/src/home/homework.c
@@ -1191,6 +1191,11 @@
                         return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(ENOKEY), "Missing plaintext password for defined hashed password");
         }
 
+        /* Recovery keys are needed in plaintext only where they are propagated into key slots, i.e. for
+         * LUKS and fscrypt. Elsewhere their hashes are carried over as they are: insisting on them would make
+         * every password change require the recovery key, which is only meant for a lost password. Whoever
+         * acts still has to prove it: the secret is authenticated against the embedded record. */
+        if (IN_SET(user_record_storage(h), USER_LUKS, USER_FSCRYPT))
         FOREACH_ARRAY(i, h->recovery_key, h->n_recovery_key) {
                 bool found = false;
 
